The most important step is soaking the[ peas] till[ it pl]umps up three times their size[. I] soak the[ peas] for a minimum of 12 – 24 hours[ to] make it[ easier to] digest[.] Change the soaking water every 3-4 hours[, till] the[ water is] clear and free of bubbles[.] Add a pinch of sea salt when soaking overnight to draw out the gas which will form bubbles on top of the water[.] Be sure to use cold water when[ rins]ing and soaking the peas. Changing the soaking water and adding some sea salt helps reduce bloating and uncomfortable gas associated with legumes.
