> North Central Service Train No. 115 collided with the vehicle around 6:10 p[.]m. near Touhy Avenue and Mannheim Road, said Met[ra] spokesman Michael[ Gillis.]
The train struck the back portion of the car, dragging it and pushing it into a[ tree].
Two of the car's passengers were taken to Advocate Lutheran General Hospital in Park Ridge, while the other injured passenger was transported to Northwest Community Hospital in Arlington Heights,[ Gill]is said. Their injuries do not appear to be life threatening.
No one on the train was hurt[.]

