> Expressing grief over the tragic incident at Kuligad Dhrabhshala in which two[ persons died], Minister of State for Transport,[ Sunil] Kumar Sharma today visited the spot to take stock of the road condition[.] The Minister along with the Superintending Engineer R&B Doda/Kishtwar/[Ram]ban,[ N]iaz Bandey, ADC Kishtwar Kishori Lal Sharma, Executive Engineer Doda, Bhush[an] Lal Thusoo and Executive Engineer Kishtwar Maninder Kumar, visited the spot to ascertain the situation and condition of road on which work is[ being initiated by NH]IDCL on war footing[ basis.]
The Minister expressed anguish over the incident and urged upon the[ authorities] to[ be] vigilant[ so] as to avoid loss of lives.[ “]All we need[ to] do[ is] better implementation with honesty,[”] he said. After the visit the Minister convened an emergency meeting with the officers at Thathri Dak Bungalow and discussed the measures for alternate road for which Executive Engineer[ R]&B has been directed to Submit DPR within days[.
